# TypeScript, TSX and the scripts that decide what a television installs are
# text, whatever byte a string literal happens to hold.
#
# Row.tsx carried a NUL as a list separator, so git classified a focus-critical
# file as binary: `git diff` said only "Binary files differ" and `grep -r` found
# nothing in it, so a review - human or automated - saw none of it. The escapes
# are fixed at the source, but the base side of a diff can still carry one, and
# one stray control character should not be able to hide a source file again.
#
# The build and publish scripts and the manifests are in here deliberately:
# they compute the sha256s a box trusts and decide what it installs, so they are
# the files it would matter most to hide.
#
# `.ts` is also the MPEG transport-stream extension. If a real media fixture
# ever lands, give its directory a `*.ts -diff` of its own rather than dropping
# this line - a stream rendered as text is noise, a hidden source file is a hole.
*.ts diff
*.tsx diff
*.js diff
*.jsx diff
*.mjs diff
*.cjs diff
*.json diff
*.css diff
*.html diff
*.md diff
*.sh diff
*.yml diff
*.yaml diff
